{
  "task_id": "T03",
  "issue": "https://github.com/Fanduzi/DeltaScope/issues/82",
  "policy_profile": "all-rules-disabled",
  "description": "Incomplete-coverage golden path: the shared parser accepts CREATE SEQUENCE but MySQL does not support it, so the statement stays in the result as incomplete coverage with bounded unsupported evidence while a supported ALTER stays complete. DB steps prove uniform CREATE/ALTER/DROP legality on all four anchors; CLI cases prove the incomplete audit contract under an all-rules-disabled policy, including --fail-on none still exiting 1, recognized-but-unaudited ALTER sub-actions and nested options, vendor boundaries, execution-capable EXPLAIN ANALYZE/TRACE/EXECUTE, and the read-only EXPLAIN counter-example, and the remaining recognized-but-unaudited boundary families: temporary-table scope (local/global, create/drop), AUTO_RANDOM column attributes, MySQL procedure bodies, dropped column options (generated/inline REFERENCES/CHECK/UNIQUE), plus ordinary-table contrasts and the procedure parser-error contract (exit 2).",
  "anchors": {
